--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SCOPE (no scope narrowing — covenant #2)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The web DevToolsPage is a thin tabbed shell: PageContainer(title + subtitle) + TabNav
(5 tabs: Fleet API / Telemetry / Infrastructure / Utilities / Reference) + a per-tab
container (<FadeIn key={tab}>) hosting one of five SIBLING components. Per the manifest
the page declares NO API data sources — it "renders from navigation values / local
state"; the five sections (FleetApiSection, FleetTelemetryHealth, InfrastructureSection,
ClientUtilitiesSection, ReferenceLinksSection) are SEPARATE, already-shipped parity
units living in TeslaSync/feature-views/*. The native page reproduces EVERY region the
web page owns — the title, the subtitle, the tab bar, and the per-tab section host —
and mounts the REAL native section views (NOT stubs, ADR-011) under each tab.

No production data source exists for the five sections yet (only their in-memory seam
sources ship; the P1/S8 production wiring is a separate, out-of-scope unit). So the
LiveDevToolsSectionProvider feeds each section through its in-memory seam, seeded to an
honest RESOLVED state (never a perpetual spinner / blank region):
  • Fleet API / Telemetry / Infrastructure / Utilities → the genuine "no live data wired
    yet" case → each section renders its OWN designed empty state.
  • Reference → backed by the static client-side ReferenceLinkCatalog.defaultLinks (the
    native port of the web `REFERENCE_LINKS` constant) → renders its real link grid,
    exactly as ApiPlayground renders its static documented-route catalog.
The page + model + tests depend only on the DevToolsSectionProviding protocol (section
wiring is isolated to the one provider file), so the page parity is independently
verifiable.

